title: Workers Are Not a Backdrop
subtitle: Nurses, teachers and union organisers want commitments they can audit.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_workers_public_services_timer <= 0 and (labor_credibility < 70 or union_trust < 70 or labor_mobilization < 60 or health_capacity < 65 or labor_dissent >= 25 or social_spending_salience >= 55)
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_workers_public_services_timer = 4
card-image: img/poland/cards/workers-public-services.webp

= Workers Are Not a Backdrop

The Left's launch spoke constantly about workers. Lewica Pracy MPs and union
representatives now ask who will enforce labour law, fund hospitals and bargain
with public servants after the launch is over. [? if razem_in_left_club = 1 and razem_split = 0:
Razem wants dates. ?][? if razem_in_left_club = 0 or razem_split = 1: Razem
attacks the parliamentary Left from outside for refusing to name dates. ?] The
old guard wants room to negotiate.

- @union_compact
- @services_guarantee
- @parliamentary_hearing

@union_compact
title: Sign an OPZZ and wider-union organising compact
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Credibility and organisers, plus another coalition red line.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A staffed organising compact requires one resource.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; labor_credibility += 5; union_trust += 8; opzz_cooperation += 8; labor_mobilization += 7; organiser_energy += 4; labor_dissent -= 5; razem_cooperation += 3; razem_dissent -= 2; progressives_dissent -= 2; spring_dissent -= 1; barons_dissent += 2; budget_promises += 1; ko_relation -= 2; government_coalition_dissent += 1 if left_in_government = 1; workers_support += 5; public_sector_support += 2; turnout_readiness += 1; primary_union_slate = 1; primary_social_slate = 1; news_headline = "OPZZ and wider-union organisers put milestones in the Left programme"

Workplace inspection, bargaining access and public-sector pay receive deadlines
and named parliamentary sponsors. The commitments can now be organised around.
They can also be used against you in December.

- #poland_card_finish

@services_guarantee
title: Guarantee health and education capacity
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Opposition creates policy pressure, not state capacity; a cabinet can implement it.
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Preparing a serious public-services guarantee costs two resources.
on-arrival: {!
const support = Number(Q.social_spending_support);
const salience = Number(Q.social_spending_salience);
const backlash = Number(Q.social_spending_backlash);
const raw = ((support - 50) / 15 - (backlash - 35) / 45) *
    (0.45 + salience / 100);
const net = Math.round(Math.max(
    -3,
    Math.min(3, raw)
));
const scale = Math.max(0.65, Math.min(1.50, 1 + net * 0.15));
Q.resources -= 2;
if (Q.left_in_government) {
    Q.health_capacity += Math.max(3, Math.round(5 * scale));
    Q.household_security += Math.max(2, Math.round(3 * scale));
    Q.government_delivery += 1;
    Q.last_policy_stage = "Cabinet implementation";
    Q.last_policy_authority = "Council of Ministers";
    Q.last_policy_implementation = "Funded public-service guarantee";
} else {
    Q.health_policy_pressure += Math.max(3, Math.round(5 * scale));
    Q.household_policy_pressure += Math.max(2, Math.round(3 * scale));
    Q.tactical_desertion_to_ko += 0.8 + Math.max(0, -net) * 0.2;
    Q.tactical_desertion_to_p2050 += 0.4 + Math.max(0, -net) * 0.15;
    Q.last_policy_stage = "Opposition programme";
    Q.last_policy_authority = "Lewica party leadership";
    Q.last_policy_implementation = "Not enacted";
}
Q.public_trust += 1 + net * 0.25;
Q.labor_credibility += Math.max(2, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.union_trust += Math.max(2, Math.round(3 * scale));
Q.opzz_cooperation += Math.max(1, Math.round(2 * scale));
Q.labor_mobilization += Math.max(1, Math.round(2 * scale));
Q.labor_dissent -= Math.max(1, Math.round(2 * scale));
Q.budget_promises += 3;
Q.barons_dissent += 2 + (net < 0 ? 1 : 0);
Q.public_sector_support += Math.max(2, Math.round(5 * scale));
Q.women_support += net >= 0 ? 1 : 0;
Q.issue_ownership += 2 + net * 0.6;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_left_ownership += 4 + net;
Q.electoral_viability += Math.max(0, net) * 0.3;
Q.primary_union_slate = 1;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += net >= 1 ? 2 : (net <= -2 ? -1 : 1);
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_salience += 6;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_backlash += net < 0 ? 4 : 2;
Q.card_public_response_score = net;
Q.card_public_response = net >= 2
    ? "breakthrough"
    : (net >= 1
        ? "favourable"
        : (net <= -2
            ? "reversal"
            : (net <= -1 ? "backlash" : "contested")));
Q.public_opinion_last_issue = "Social spending and public services";
Q.public_opinion_last_reception = Q.card_public_response;
Q.public_opinion_last_delta = net;
Q.public_opinion_last_action = "Public-services guarantee";
Q.story_queue = Array.isArray(Q.story_queue) ? Q.story_queue : [];
Q.story_queue.push({
    title: "Public-services guarantee",
    issue: "social_spending",
    label: "Social spending and public services",
    reach: Math.min(100, 38 + Number(Q.media_capacity) * 0.72),
    audienceTrust: Number(Q.public_trust),
    frame: net >= 0 ? 54 + net * 14 : -54 + net * 14,
    messengerCredibility:
        (Number(Q.labor_credibility) + Number(Q.public_trust)) / 2,
    issueSalience: salience,
    leftCredibility:
        (Number(Q.labor_credibility) + Number(Q.issue_ownership)) / 2
});
Q.news_headline = net >= 1
    ? "A measurable services guarantee meets a public demand"
    : (net <= -1
        ? "The services guarantee opens an immediate cost fight"
        : "The Left makes public services a measurable guarantee");
!}

[? if card_public_response = "breakthrough": The plan specifies staffing,
local access and emergency reserves at precisely the moment voters are looking
for an alternative to decline. A future budget obligation becomes an immediate
political asset. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "favourable": Concrete staffing and access
commitments are popular enough to survive the first cost questions. The bill
will still arrive in December. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "contested": The guarantee looks governable and
expensive in equal measure. It cannot be funded by a clever press release. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "backlash": The service case wins the committed
audience, but fiscal alarm dominates the wider coverage. December begins
early. ?]
[? if card_public_response = "reversal": Public anxiety has hardened into
distrust of new promises. The guarantee creates a liability until the Left can
show where the money and staff come from. ?]

- #poland_card_finish

@parliamentary_hearing
title: Give workers a parliamentary hearing
subtitle: Free and visible, but weaker than the commitment organisers requested.
on-arrival: labor_credibility += 2; union_trust -= 3; opzz_cooperation -= 2; public_trust += 0; health_policy_pressure += 1; media_capacity += 1; razem_dissent += 3; labor_dissent += 2; workers_support += 2; public_sector_support += 2; tactical_desertion_to_abstention += 0.5; last_policy_stage = "Advocacy"; last_policy_authority = "Party hearing"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Workers testify while the Left postpones its guarantees"

The testimony reaches television and exposes familiar abuses. The caucus
promises to return with legislation. Union representatives have heard that
sentence before.

- #poland_card_finish
